.UPDATE...
Issued at 632 AM PDT Wed Sep 16 2026

The marine layer has grown to roughly 2,400 feet deep this
morning, with widespread stratus coverage. The NW wind direction
is supporting downslope drying over the Santa Cruz mountains,
which is keeping Silicon Valley clear. Otherwise the morning
clouds are reaching as far as Healdsburg, Dublin, and Pacheco
Pass. There hasn`t been any measurable drizzle yet. The clouds
will start to pull back to the coast after the sun comes up.

