.LONG TERM...
Issued at 1250 AM PDT Wed Sep 16 2026
(Thursday through Tuesday)

Cloudy, cool, damp to begin the day on Thursday as the upper low
lingers over NorCal. By Friday, the cut-off low exits to the NE
with a weak shortwave ridge following for Saturday. This shift in
the upper level pattern will have a shift in the sensible weather.
The marine layer will compress slightly and temperatures will
warm.

Longer range is lower confidence as yet another upper low begins
to move through CA Monday. Expect another dip in temperatures, but
albeit brief. Thereafter, the strength of the following ridge is
uncertain. Regardless, current forecast does show warming through
the middle of next week.

