.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 1024 AM PDT Wed Sep 16 2026

An interesting stratus pattern across the region today. Stratus
should clear within the hour at STS and APC with questions as to
if OAK and SFO will clear at all today. Model guidance suggests
patchy reductions in cloud cover are possible for OAK, SFO, MRY,
and SNS with the general prevailing conditions being MVFR. Kept
the TAFs slightly more pessimistic with MVFR conditions prevailing
through the day but there may be brief periods where cloud cover
is reduced and conditions improve during the day. Breezy onshore
winds are expected this afternoon and evening with winds between
10 to 15 knots and gusts to around 25 knots at OAK and SFO. With
the marine layer deepening to 3000 ft tonight it is likely that
OVC/BKN clouds will be at a higher depth tonight. This may result
in cloud cover on the border of MVFR / VFR criteria.

Vicinity of SFO...Stratus continues to push into SFO after
clearing briefly earlier this morning. Maintained a slightly more
optimistic TAF with VFR returning this afternoon. MVFR conditions
return late tonight and prevail through tomorrow morning. Gusts to
around 25 knots are expected this afternoon.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...MVFR conditions at both sites. Given the
continued push of stratus towards the interior, kept MVFR
conditions prevailing through the day at both sites. This may need
to be adjusted if cloud cover is able to break up more than
originally anticipated. Breezy westerly winds between 10 to 15
knots expected this afternoon with lighter winds overnight.

