.MARINE...
(Today through Monday)
Issued at 1024 AM PDT Wed Sep 16 2026

Moderate northwest to north winds prevail across the outer waters
with occasional fresh to strong gusts to diminish today. West to
southwest moderate breezes dominate over the Bays with gusts up to
25 knots resulting in hazardous conditions for small crafts late
morning through this evening. By Friday, widespread northwest to
north breezes increase to fresh with occasional strong gusts.
Wind driven rough seas to 9 to 10 feet subside to moderate by the
evening and will remain slight to moderate into the weekend.

